WEBVTT

00:25:29.581 --> 00:25:33.232
There's a study of a couple a hundred
Silicon Valley start-ups

00:25:33.256 --> 00:25:36.435
where Jim Baron and his colleagues

00:25:36.459 --> 00:25:38.490
identified the cultural blueprints,

00:25:38.514 --> 00:25:41.871
and they found that if you,
as a founder, had a blueprint

00:25:41.895 --> 00:25:46.364
where you were going to convince people
that you had an important mission

00:25:46.388 --> 00:25:49.190
and everyone was going to be
passionate about that mission

00:25:49.214 --> 00:25:52.325
and the culture was organized
around commitment,

00:25:52.349 --> 00:25:55.099
that your start-up
was less likely to fail,

00:25:55.123 --> 00:25:58.968
and it was also significantly
more likely to have an IPO.

00:25:58.992 --> 00:26:00.805
But then post-IPO,